# A Dragoon loses to an undefended colony's militia: the attack still spends its whole allotment
# (1b0e's entry FUN_281f_0934, port_bugs.md #1375), so the demoted Soldiers (spent 12) give way
# to the next unit instead of attacking again.
# Start: map_attack_colony_capture's input.sav (France, Spring 1600, at war with England; veteran
# Dragoons #131 and #87 at (39,23) east of English Cayenne (38,23, pop 2, no unit on its tile),
# #131 active, Combat Analysis on). Rolls come from the saved LCG, so the outcome is fixed.
key KP_4                 # #131 attacks Cayenne: the colony militia phantom fights; analysis
wait 3
key Return               # dismiss: roll lost
wait 3
key Return               # "{French Dragoons} routed! Unit demoted to {Soldiers} status."
wait 3
key Return               # "{English Colonists} defeat {French} near Cayenne!"; #87 selected next
wait 3
shot
